      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it will block for 5 seconds in this case.  I cannot use a yield asleep in a streaming method.  This was the exact same case with Voltha before. Now that I enabled streaming RPC on both sides (i.e. ofagent and voltha), the blocking is done on the ofagent side only.  As for Voltha, it will simply wait for the next available subscription request and not block anything else.",
